cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "autoqec-sim: circuit-level evaluation of stabilizer codes under device noise"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-16"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/unitaryfoundation/autoqec-sim"
keywords:
  - quantum error correction
  - stabilizer codes
  - logical error rate
  - device noise models
  - reinforcement learning
  - Clifford simulation
abstract: >-
  Circuit-level evaluation of stabilizer codes under device noise: one call
  builds the syndrome-extraction memory experiment of any stabilizer code,
  applies a noise model with sourced device parameters, and returns the
  logical error per round, the exact circuit-level distance, and the
  dominant fault sets, without sampling or a decoder. With the proposers
  that generate candidates: a SAT-population pipeline, an evolutionary
  search, and a PPO agent on a batched Aaronson-Gottesman tableau, and the
  rediscovery regressions that verify what they find.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Simultaneous discovery of quantum error correction codes and encoders with a noise-aware reinforcement learning agent"
